The new Blink comes with an added feature for generating resident
libraries. Here's how to do it:
  
1) Make sure that all modules in the library are compiled with the
   "-ml" option and use the "__saveds" keyword (or -y option). "-b0"
    is not allowed.
    
2) Create a .fd file for your library.

3) Link with the command line:

blink LIBPREFIX _LIB LIBFD fdfile TO libname FROM libent.o libinit.o libmodules

where 
    LIBPREFIX is an optional keyword that specifies what prefix to add the
              the functions listed in the .fd file. _LIB is the prefix in 
	      this example. The default is simply an _. Note that without 
	      this keyword, you can't use stubs to call this library. Also
	      remember that the compiler adds an underscore to everything so
	      if you define your function as _LIBtest() in your C code,
	      the prefix should be __LIB.
	      
    LIBFD is a new keyword used to specify the name of the .fd file (fdfile).

    libent.o contains the RomTag for the library, MUST BE FIRST (ala c.o).

    libinit.o contains Open, Close, Expunge, and other init stuff,
              MUST BE THE SECOND MODULE.

    libmodules are user modules.
		
   

